\section{Method Selection Guide}
\label{app:method_selection}

The M1/M2 diagnostic framework guides practitioners toward the appropriate fix without exhaustive ablation. If only M2 is active (sign misattribution with sufficient observation context, e.g., $h$ large enough to preserve task-relevant information), per-step credit methods---Turn-PPO~\cite{turnppo2025}, HCAPO~\cite{hcapo2026}, GiGPO~\cite{feng2025gigpo}---directly address the failure mode. If only M1 is active (information loss without sign corruption), increasing $h$ or switching to full-context encoding suffices. When both co-occur (the typical default configuration), episode-level methods address both simultaneously. Finer-grained credit methods should be applied only after establishing an episode-level baseline, as they assume correct gradient direction.

